1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,478
This is the last lecture of the class,

2
00:00:03,928 --> 00:00:06,972
and it puts the whole class together.

3
00:00:07,872 --> 00:00:12,654
You have a boss, with ships and objectives and a hook.

4
00:00:13,104 --> 00:00:18,757
And you know how to write a scene, a call, and an answer.

5
00:00:20,557 --> 00:00:22,730
Today, at last, she speaks.

6
00:00:23,630 --> 00:00:30,587
And along the way, you'll find the one hard limit in everything you've learned so far.

7
00:00:31,787 --> 00:00:36,570
Last time, the crew had ten minutes to sink the Morrigan,

8
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:40,933
and nothing warned them as the time ran down.

9
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:43,572
Two lines fix that.

10
00:00:44,472 --> 00:00:47,080
Speaker says who gives the warning,

11
00:00:47,530 --> 00:00:53,183
and here it's a role: the name of her flagship, in small letters.

12
00:00:54,083 --> 00:00:56,691
Signal says is what she sends.

13
00:00:58,491 --> 00:01:02,404
Where I write the word time, in curly brackets,

14
00:01:02,854 --> 00:01:06,333
the game puts in the time that's left.

15
00:01:07,233 --> 00:01:12,885
It's sent at five minutes, at two, at one, and at thirty seconds,

16
00:01:13,335 --> 00:01:17,248
and only the ones that fit inside your limit.

17
00:01:18,448 --> 00:01:21,057
Now run lint, and it complains.

18
00:01:21,957 --> 00:01:25,000
It says morrigan isn't in the cast.

19
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:30,713
And for a boss file, that warning is wrong.

20
00:01:31,613 --> 00:01:34,222
Lint's looking for a Characters section,

21
00:01:34,672 --> 00:01:37,715
and a boss file hasn't got one.

22
00:01:38,615 --> 00:01:41,659
The game looks for a character first,

23
00:01:42,109 --> 00:01:47,326
and then for a ship wearing that role, and it finds her.

24
00:01:48,226 --> 00:01:55,183
So this is the only warning in the whole course that I'll tell you to keep.

25
00:01:56,083 --> 00:01:58,257
Read it every time, though.

26
00:01:58,707 --> 00:02:04,359
If the name in it isn't on your Named line, then it's true.

27
00:02:05,559 --> 00:02:09,472
For testing, I've set the limit to three minutes.

28
00:02:10,372 --> 00:02:12,980
She arrives, and I do nothing.

29
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:18,663
About a minute later, Comms gets a message from the Morrigan,

30
00:02:19,113 --> 00:02:22,157
with the objective's name as its title.

31
00:02:23,957 --> 00:02:26,565
You have one fifty-nine, little ship.

32
00:02:27,015 --> 00:02:29,189
Then this sector is mine.

33
00:02:30,089 --> 00:02:32,698
That's her voice, in my words,

34
00:02:33,148 --> 00:02:35,757
and it's in the one file.

35
00:02:36,657 --> 00:02:41,874
If I send that file to a friend, they hear it too.

36
00:02:43,074 --> 00:02:47,857
So you'd think the call goes in that file as well.

37
00:02:48,757 --> 00:02:54,409
A Characters section, a Dialogue section, and a Beat to place the call.

38
00:02:56,209 --> 00:03:00,557
It doesn't work, and I want you to see why.

39
00:03:01,457 --> 00:03:05,370
The Siege reads a boss file for two things:

40
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:08,428
the boss's own lines, and quests.

41
00:03:09,328 --> 00:03:13,241
Everything under the boss is treated as a quest.

42
00:03:14,141 --> 00:03:20,663
So your cast and your scenes turn up in the crew's quest lists, as jobs,

43
00:03:21,113 --> 00:03:23,287
and no call ever comes.

44
00:03:24,187 --> 00:03:26,796
And lint doesn't say a word.

45
00:03:27,996 --> 00:03:33,213
So her cast and her scenes get a file of their own,

46
00:03:33,663 --> 00:03:36,707
in the folder you made last time.

47
00:03:37,607 --> 00:03:39,780
It's a small mission file.

48
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,854
It has a title line,

49
00:03:43,304 --> 00:03:46,783
a Characters section with the Queen in it,

50
00:03:47,233 --> 00:03:50,276
and a Dialogue section with one scene.

51
00:03:52,076 --> 00:03:56,424
The scene is exactly what you wrote in Lecture 3.

52
00:03:56,874 --> 00:04:00,787
A speaker, two blocks of takes, and an answer.

53
00:04:01,687 --> 00:04:05,165
And that answer finishes a quest called parley,

54
00:04:05,615 --> 00:04:07,789
which we haven't written yet.

55
00:04:08,989 --> 00:04:13,337
Something has to read that file, and that's her card.

56
00:04:14,237 --> 00:04:18,150
Three lines, and you copy them as they are.

57
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:21,224
The first opens the file.

58
00:04:21,674 --> 00:04:25,152
The second brings its people into the game,

59
00:04:25,602 --> 00:04:29,950
and the third makes its scenes ready to be called.

60
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:34,359
You've seen the last two before,

61
00:04:34,809 --> 00:04:38,287
because your own mission's story file has them.

62
00:04:39,187 --> 00:04:43,100
One rule: they go first, right under the label.

63
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,478
The call is placed the moment she arrives,

64
00:04:47,928 --> 00:04:52,276
so the scenes have to be read before anything waits.

65
00:04:53,476 --> 00:04:58,693
The call is placed the way you placed one in Lecture 5:

66
00:04:59,143 --> 00:05:05,230
a Beat, with an Action line that says, queen hails, and the scene's key.

67
00:05:06,130 --> 00:05:08,739
It goes in the boss file,

68
00:05:09,189 --> 00:05:11,798
because that's where her quests are.

69
00:05:13,598 --> 00:05:15,772
Now the answer that matters.

70
00:05:16,672 --> 00:05:20,150
A second answer leads to a second scene,

71
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:24,513
where the Badb's first mate comes on the line.

72
00:05:25,413 --> 00:05:29,326
And if the crew says, then fly with us,

73
00:05:29,776 --> 00:05:32,385
three things happen after the semicolon.

74
00:05:33,285 --> 00:05:35,024
The call is finished.

75
00:05:35,474 --> 00:05:39,822
Turn the Badb is finished, which reveals one more step.

76
00:05:40,272 --> 00:05:44,185
And that step has an Action of its own:

77
00:05:44,635 --> 00:05:46,809
badb joins T S N.

78
00:05:47,709 --> 00:05:49,883
So the ship changes sides.

79
00:05:51,083 --> 00:05:54,126
Check both files, and then play it.

80
00:05:55,026 --> 00:05:59,374
There's her call, waiting, with her name and the title.

81
00:06:00,274 --> 00:06:03,317
I open it, she makes her offer,

82
00:06:03,767 --> 00:06:06,811
and I talk to the Badb instead.

83
00:06:08,611 --> 00:06:10,350
Then fly with us.

84
00:06:11,250 --> 00:06:16,033
The crew's told the call is done, the Badb is turned,

85
00:06:16,483 --> 00:06:19,961
and the bonus for sinking her is closed.

86
00:06:20,861 --> 00:06:22,600
That's a real choice:

87
00:06:23,050 --> 00:06:26,093
three hundred credits, or one raider fewer.

88
00:06:26,993 --> 00:06:30,037
Then play it again and refuse her,

89
00:06:30,487 --> 00:06:35,270
and play it a third time and never answer at all.

90
00:06:36,170 --> 00:06:40,083
The game has to be winnable on every road.

91
00:06:41,283 --> 00:06:44,761
Now be honest about what you're handing over.

92
00:06:45,661 --> 00:06:48,270
If you send the one file,

93
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:52,633
your friend gets the boss, her ships, her objectives,

94
00:06:53,083 --> 00:06:55,691
and the Morrigan calling the clock.

95
00:06:56,591 --> 00:07:01,809
They don't get the arrival line, the reserve ship, or the call.

96
00:07:03,609 --> 00:07:08,391
For those, they need the folder too, inside their Legendary Missions.

97
00:07:09,291 --> 00:07:14,074
And an update removes that folder, for them and for you.

98
00:07:14,974 --> 00:07:18,017
So keep a copy outside the game,

99
00:07:18,467 --> 00:07:21,511
and put it back when it's gone.

100
00:07:22,411 --> 00:07:26,759
Lint will tell you: one warning when the folder's there,

101
00:07:27,209 --> 00:07:29,383
and three when it isn't.

102
00:07:30,583 --> 00:07:33,191
The page ends with a rubric,

103
00:07:33,641 --> 00:07:38,424
and every line on it is something you can check yourself.

104
00:07:39,324 --> 00:07:43,237
She's yours, she's checked, she plays, and she travels.

105
00:07:45,037 --> 00:07:48,950
When every line is ticked, you've finished Class 2.

106
00:07:49,850 --> 00:07:52,893
You can write a cast, a conversation,

107
00:07:53,343 --> 00:07:55,952
and a boss who talks back.

108
00:07:56,852 --> 00:08:00,765
In the next class, the crew leaves the bridge.
